{"Automated refactor swapped lightness values inconsistently across desktop/mobile - multiple selectors have primary-branch lightness values changed (e.g. 30%\u219270% or 70%\u219230%) and desktop vs mobile counterparts for the same element use inverted lightness pairs": 0.839362382888794, "dark-light-choose function has inverted logic - returns $light-theme-result when brightness($primary) < brightness($secondary), which is the dark-theme condition, causing wrong colors in dark themes": 0.28645551204681396, "Existing call sites pass reversed args to dark-light-choose (secondary, primary) to compensate for current semantics, but PR's bulk replacement uses (primary, secondary) order without preserving that compensation, creating inconsistent behavior across stylesheets": 0.29515746235847473, "search-highlight uses asymmetric 25%/75% lightness values in dark-light-choose call - if dark-light-choose has inverted logic, highlights will display wrong colors, and this edge case needs specific test coverage": 0.5089304447174072}